WEBVTT

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.520
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.660
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.730
Do they want to protect themselves or other people? Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.690
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.300
To an endless, eternal picture of hell,

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.490
pushing through time, a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.430
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.040
<i>I am inside of you.</i>

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.290
Why?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.730
Were you surprised?

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.870
Akie…

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:56.890
Caged Bird

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.850
Yuurisan-Subs & マイワイフ Subs

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.850
http://yuurisan-subs.org
http://maiwaifufansubs.wordpress.com

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.850
Sub Dedicated to Enma Ai

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.910
You seem down.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.710
Really?

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.020
Is it still bothering you?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.380
The Itsuko incident?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.140
What?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.920
Y-Yeah.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.200
It doesn’t concern you, Yuzuki,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.920
since Itsuko has so much pride.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.860
I didn’t think she would change schools, though.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:04.390
Although,

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.910
we worried so much about Tange-sensei, right?

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.840
He probably didn’t feel comfortable anymore.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.260
I wonder where Tange-sensei went?

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.130
He said that the “amigos” were an elopement,

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.780
but that can’t be true.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.790
Since no matter how you look at him…

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.880
Sorry! I have something to do.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.240
What? Can you wait a bit? Yuzuki!

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.380
Hey, look who I found!

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.630
Amigos!

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.480
What are you doing? Are you alone?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:39.540
Ah, well.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.490
We’re going out for cake.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.010
Akie-chan, do you want to come, too?

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.850
Yeah, I’ll come!

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.990
Good! Let’s go then!

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.170
Good evening, Akira-kun.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.170
Akira-kun?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:12.730
Yes?

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.300
Yes. Ok, then,

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.080
but I have a customer waiting, so…

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.360
I’m sorry!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.580
Always keeping you waiting.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.320
Uh oh, looks like we’re out.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.380
Are you fine with AA?

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:41.880
Yes.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.160
Yesterday and today were both AA as well…

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.350
Oh, I’m sorry, looks like I’ve said too much.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.790
That’ll be 47 yen.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.480
I use it with so many things.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.040
Oh, right, of course.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.640
What’s wrong?

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.390
Well…

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.720
Not enough?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:09.440
Yeah…

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.440
How much do you need?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:21.320
46 yen… 1 yen?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.680
I’ll give it to you anyway.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.030
What? But…

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.730
Since you buy them so often,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.390
I’ll take a yen off.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.830
It’s so warm!

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.510
Thank you always.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.850
Welcome!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.050
You…

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.190
That child, since he didn’t have enough money…

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.610
I’m sorry!

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:00.820
I’m sorry!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.390
I’m sorry!

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.930
Don’t make so much noise, you idiot!

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:05.880
The whole neighborhood will hear us!

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.840
You were making eyes at that kid.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:13.540
Right?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.390
Mitsuko.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.360
Since when, huh?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.500
Not at all, that’s not what I meant!

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.840
Next time he comes, I’ll chase him home.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:23.840
But…

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.950
Since he’s a customer…

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.690
He’s no customer!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.830
Well?

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.830
Yes.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:40.650
That guy…

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:45.310
I found it!

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.560
Your grudge shall be released.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.820
Yamaoka

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.150
That man…

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.540
What’s his name?

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:07.960
Akira-kun…

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:27.810
Yes,

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.540
this is Yamaoka Electronics.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.670
It’s me.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:31.550
Yes.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.830
You’re there, like you’re supposed to be.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.360
What about the customers?

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.320
None yet.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.220
I’ll call again later.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.010
<font size=77>Yamaoka Seiji
 Mitsuko

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.520
Seiji…  right.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.610
Success, success!

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:06.380
Nice face!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.850
I’m glad you knew about Jigoku Shoujo.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:10.550
Yeah!{,yeah!}

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:11.920
You two…

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.510
Tell us if you have a grudge on somebody!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:18.930
We the Hell Boy Corps{/Guys} will give the cursed straw doll as a present.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.610
Ouch!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.610
You idiots!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.910
Wait, what? Just…

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.170
What was that for?

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:31.060
Is there a reason to get so mad?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.840
You should try dying once!

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.890
I’ll ask again.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.390
After three, you answered the phone late.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.140
I wonder why?

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.740
I already told you, I was taking in the laundry-

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:54.780
Don’t fucking lie to me!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.320
I know, I know what’s going on.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.400
You were baiting that kid, weren’t you?

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:07.810
I’m telling the truth… the laundry…

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.400
Now tell me the truth,

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.210
Mitsuko!

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.320
Watch me.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.270
Your grudge shall be released.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:20.260
Yamaoka Seiji

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.490
Yamaoka Seiji

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:34.440
I’m here.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.260
J-Jigoku Shoujo.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.700
Hey, kid!

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:43.710
Wanyuudou.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.200
Yes, Ojou.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.580
Take this.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:56.780
If you really want to release your grudge,

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.980
just pull the red string.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.530
If you pull the string,

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.490
it would mean you’ll sign a contract with me.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:09.010
The object of your grudge will promptly be sent to hell.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:12.830
However,

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:17.490
there is a price.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.310
If you curse one person,

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:25.970
two holes are created. If you sign the contract, your soul will fall to hell, too.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.880
Only after you die.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:32.000
Me too…

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.380
to hell…

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.170
The rest is up to you.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.070
Why…

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.560
…do you show me?

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.810
Why, Jigoku Shoujo?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.010
Today’s horoscope…

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.260
Oh, father?

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:15.030
Sorry it’s early.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.300
I wanted to hear your voice.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.350
How is it over there? Is Mother well?

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.290
Yes, yes.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:30.330
Yes, I’m fine.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:35.710
Can I take a bit of your time?

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:37.820
What?

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:44.300
My friend asked me to ask you something.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:48.140
And,

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.310
how much does he like her?

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.090
 What?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.390
That friend…

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.350
How much? Well…

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:01.390
I understand the feeling that he wants to help that mistreated woman, but…

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.980
I think that man’s serious.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.130
Oh…

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:13.470
Right, something should be done about him?

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:14.590
Something?

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.620
That is…

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:23.650
That woman, I wonder if she hates that man?

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.110
Of course she hates him!

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:28.740
She’s being mistreated everyday!

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.600
Then, I wonder why she isn’t running away?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.110
She can’t.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:35.540
Even if she does, he chases her,

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.970
and then mistreats her even more!

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:40.610
He’s that sort of guy! That man!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.790
I haven’t met him,

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.830
but I bet he’s like that.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.860
Then, Akira-kun,

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:55.430
what does that woman think of your friend?

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:56.880
What?

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.610
Did she tell him she liked him?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.640
Akira-kun,

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.410
tell that friend,

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.530
maybe it’s better if he didn’t meddle anymore.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:10.940
What?

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.710
I don’t understand that well,

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.660
but I think liking someone has many different forms.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.320
That woman probably…

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:25.850
No, that’s wrong.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:27.940
She…

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:30.740
wants to escape!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.850
Akira-kun!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:42.590
Hey,

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.990
I wonder why Ojou picked her?

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.980
On a whim, I suppose.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.280
I mean, it’s not even you.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.220
I can’t agree with you there.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:55.010
It’s possible that she’s borrowed lodging.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:57.980
Since it’s probably easier to move around in a human body instead of a butterfly.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:03.220
Yeah, since you can’t do anything but attach yourself to something, if you don’t have a real body.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.560
Well, we’ll find out eventually.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.210
Let’s watch for a while.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.030
I wonder…

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:15.860
if something accursed is going to happen in this city…

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:34.020
Y-You?

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:39.050
Come on, don’t frighten me!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.050
Um…

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.050
What happened to school?

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.330
It’s not over yet, is it?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.090
Um…

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:09.180
Something bad happened at school, didn’t it?

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.990
That’s not good, skipping school!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.110
Come on, go back to school!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:16.990
I know.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.870
That’s from a rope, isn’t it?

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.470
Why?

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:33.470
Let go of me.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.380
Don’t answer a call from that bastard.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:36.770
But…

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.340
There’s no reason to become his servant!

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.540
Please…

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.460
Let go!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.740
He hung up…

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.560
Why do you tolerate this?

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:56.720
Run away!

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.470
There’s no reason to say with someone like him!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.070
Leave now!

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.800
If you don’t have a place to go,

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:09.470
you can come to my place! I’ll make my parents understand.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:12.570
Yeah, come to my place!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:15.140
You, is that why you came?

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.220
Skipping school, to say that?

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:27.600
Thanks…

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.250
Then, together…

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:32.400
Why?!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:35.030
Go, that man’s coming back.

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:38.100
If he finds you, you’ll be in grave danger. Hurry.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.150
No! Come with me!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.040
You bastard!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:54.150
Stop it! I’m sorry!

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.620
It’s my fault! It’s my-

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:56.260
Shut up!

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:04.880
I’m sorry, it’s my fault, so don’t…

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.840
You were baiting him after all, weren’t you?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.580
No, I wasn’t…

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.700
Run away… quickly…

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.130
Stop!

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:22.630
You were baiting him, right? Right?

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.710
<i> Your soul will also be sent to hell.</i>

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.230
Run away!

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.310
Hurry!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.380
Your grudge… is granted.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:03.120
It’s hot… Where am I?

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.700
What the hell is this?!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.560
I feel refreshed!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.720
It burns! It burns!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.230
Dinnertime!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.760
Yeah!

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:32.280
Kikuri’s enjoying this!

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:34.950
It sure is hot today!

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.850
You’re using too much electricity!

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:41.250
Hey, the Microwave’s not plugged in.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:45.750
Oh, I’m sorry! Your dad has the plug. {Wanyuudou speaking in third-person}

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:48.930
This won’t work! This is absolutely impossible!

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:50.710
Let’s go!

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.420
Take this!

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:54.830
Stop!

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.930
Don’t joke with me! What did I do?

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.420
Weren’t you mistreating your wife?

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:08.400
I wasn’t mistreating her,

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:11.090
I…  I was only trying to protect her!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.610
Protecting her, eh?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:19.820
Everything was for her, everything was for my wife!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.570
So he says, Ojou.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:24.300
Right.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.990
Any more than this… is impossible!

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:36.130
Trapped in darkness, O pitiful shadow…

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.600
Hurting people, and degrading them…

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.570
Drowned in sin is the ball of karma.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:48.100
Do you want try dying this once?

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:49.980
Use your electricity carefully!

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:02.760
Hey,

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:07.280
where’s the phone? I need to phone her! Hey!

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:09.790
Where’s the phone?! Let me borrow one! Hey!

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:11.380
Hey!

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:12.510
This hate…

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:12.510
Hey!

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.310
will send you to hell.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.300
Can’t you hear me? Hey!

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:33.860
It’s all fine now.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:37.720
Go home.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:38.480
What?

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.280
Come again tomorrow.

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:43.800
…tomorrow?

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:52.390
Right, I understand. I’ll come by before school.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:53.620
I’ll be waiting.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.210
Well, see you tomorrow then.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:08.300
The next morning,

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:12.760
the woman from the electronics store had disappeared.

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:48.790
I’ll release the grudge that you can’t.

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:48.790
Note: Candle says, Kitayama Akira.

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:46.350
Preview

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:46.350
Preview

00:24:20.710 --> 00:24:21.790
Your name?

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:23.790
Momota Masako.

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:26.290
Your grudge seems deep-rooted.

00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:31.900
I mean, she says that she’s finally regretting what she did before,

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:37.830
so I should forgive her. That’s just asking for too much!

00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:42.280
How does she think I felt? Because of that… I will never forgive her!

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:43.800
Send her to hell!

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:46.350
Your grudge… is granted.

00:24:46.350 --> 00:24:49.750
The Rotten Fruit

